p='cmd/entire/cli/agent/permissions.go'
s=open(p).read()
s=s.replace('''// Unlike the detector above, this one returns its errors, and `entire doctor`
// calls it directly rather than behind the detector: a config that cannot be
// parsed is the answer the user needs, and gating this on the detector — which
// answers false for an unreadable file — made that error unreachable.
//
// An absent config is not an error: the agent was simply never set up here.''','''// Unlike the detector above, this one returns its errors, and `entire doctor`
// calls it directly rather than behind the detector — reading and parsing the
// same file twice bought nothing, since `changed` already reports whether the
// rule was there.
//
// An absent config is not an error: the agent was simply never set up here.''',1)
open(p,'w').write(s)
